  "generated_model": "Let:\n- I = {S1, S2, ..., S12} be the set of suppliers.\n- J = {C1, C2, ..., C12} be the set of supermarkets.\n\nParameters:\n- Fixed costs for each supplier i ∈ I:\n  - f = [98.88, 99.73, 94.01, 93.77, 107.59, 112.65, 97.05, 103, 90.45, 96.73, 96.43, 112.19]\n    - f_i is the fixed cost for supplier S_i (i = 1,...,12).\n- Demand for each supermarket j ∈ J:\n  - d = [1097, 61, 11, 7, 82, 37, 483, 582, 223, 89, 60, 55]\n    - d_j is the demand for supermarket C_j (j = 1,...,12).\n- Transportation cost per unit from supplier i to supermarket j:\n  - c_ij is given by the following 12x12 matrix (rows: S1–S12, columns: C1–C12):\n\n|      |  C1    |   C2   |   C3   |   C4   |   C5   |   C6   |   C7   |   C8   |   C9   |  C10   |  C11   |  C12   |\n|------|--------|--------|--------|--------|--------|--------|--------|--------|--------|--------|--------|--------|\n| S1   | 284.11 | 53.78  | 10.62  | 111.27 | 158.5  | 8.79   | 53.79  | 8.84   | 1911.43| 8.87   |1129.47 |185.53  |\n| S2   | 7.19   |1031.96 | 90.94  | 276.97 | 0.45   | 0.2    | 49.14  | 1.05   |2079.54 | 1.45   | 49.14  | 0.05   |\n| S3   |151.10  | 884.48 | 4.33   | 277.04 | 0.33   | 0.19   | 49.14  | 0.99   | 99.03  | 1.63   | 884.47 | 0.96   |\n| S4   |144.16  | 868.75 | 94.20  | 285.48 | 16.93  | 0.94   | 868.78 | 16.60  | 98.69  |19.74   | 868.74 |19.85   |\n| S5   |151.34  |1030.88 | 91.43  | 13.24  | 0.72   | 0.87   | 49.09  | 0.01   | 99.05  | 0.84   | 883.60 | 0.58   |\n| S6   | 7.18   | 49.13  | 90.72  |277.57  | 0.37   | 0.58   |1031.74 | 0.76   |1782.98 | 1.06   | 884.31 | 0.34   |\n| S7   |104.38  |1324.35 |1829.39 |1857.57 |1782.69 |2079.47 |1324.31 |2080.29 | 0      |2080.99 |1545.08 |99.07   |\n| S8   |129.51  |1031.96 | 4.33   |276.97  | 0.02   | 0.23   |884.56  | 1.22   |2079.54 | 1.69   | 49.14  | 0.05   |\n| S9   | 50.93  | 5.75   |1057.85 | 58.62  | 47.63  |1000.41 |103.48  | 47.60  |1642.85 |47.59   | 5.75   |999.94  |\n| S10  |129.62  | 884.35 | 91.10  |277.12  | 0.27   | 0.07   |1031.78 | 0.91   | 99.03  | 0.08   | 49.13  | 0.04   |\n| S11  | 53.30  | 0      | 941.91 | 58.92  |1031.61 | 49.13  | 0.03   |1030.99 |1324.29 |49.10   | 0.08   |49.12   |\n| S12  |959.55  | 0.11   | 941.98 |1237.42 | 49.13  |1031.86 | 0.09   |1031.07 | 73.57  |49.10   | 0.12   |1031.53 |\n\nDecision variables:\n- y_i ∈ {0,1} for i = 1,...,12: y_i = 1 if supplier S_i is open, 0 otherwise.\n- x_ij ≥ 0 for i = 1,...,12, j = 1,...,12: quantity of goods supplied from S_i to C_j.\n\nModel:\n\nObjective:\nMinimize total cost (fixed + transportation):\n\\[\n\\min \\sum_{i=1}^{12} f_i y_i + \\sum_{i=1}^{12} \\sum_{j=1}^{12} c_{ij} x_{ij}\n\\]\nwhere:\n- f_i: fixed cost for supplier S_i (see vector above)\n- c_{ij}: transportation cost per unit from S_i to C_j (see matrix above)\n- y_i: binary variable for opening supplier S_i\n- x_{ij}: quantity supplied from S_i to C_j\n\nSubject to:\n\n1. Demand satisfaction for each supermarket:\n\\[\n\\sum_{i=1}^{12} x_{ij} = d_j \\quad \\forall j = 1,...,12\n\\]\nwhere d_j is the demand for supermarket C_j (see vector above).\n\n2. Supply only from open suppliers:\n\\[\nx_{ij} \\leq d_j y_i \\quad \\forall i = 1,...,12, \\forall j = 1,...,12\n\\]\nThis ensures that if y_i = 0, then x_{ij} = 0 for all j.\n\n3. Variable domains:\n\\[\ny_i \\in \\{0,1\\} \\quad \\forall i = 1,...,12\n\\]\n\\[\nx_{ij} \\geq 0 \\quad \\forall i = 1,...,12, \\forall j = 1,...,12\n\\]\n\nSummary of parameters:\n- Suppliers: S1, S2, ..., S12\n- Supermarkets: C1, C2, ..., C12\n- Fixed costs: [98.88, 99.73, 94.01, 93.77, 107.59, 112.65, 97.05, 103, 90.45, 96.73, 96.43, 112.19]\n- Demands: [1097, 61, 11, 7, 82, 37, 483, 582, 223, 89, 60, 55]\n- Transportation cost matrix: as above.\n\nThis model determines which suppliers to open (y_i) and how much each supermarket sources from each supplier (x_ij) to minimize the total cost while meeting all supermarket demands.",
